WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.630
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为您制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉您的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.550
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:26.060
Hello, everybody.
大家好。

9
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.800
Hi, you guys.
嘿，各位。

10
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.180
We have a very exciting episode today.
今天我们要聊一集非常精彩的剧集。

11
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:34.500
It is Season 4, Episode 15, Night Out.
这是第四季第十五集，《夜游》。

12
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:35.680
Yeah.
没错。

13
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.780
We traveled.
我们出差了。

14
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:37.960
We went on the road.
我们去外景地拍摄了。

15
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.040
There was locations and tons of extras.
那里有外景地和大量的临时演员。

16
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.780
This was a big production for us.
这对我们来说是一次大制作。

17
00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.020
Very little happens in The Office.
《办公室》里很少发生这种事。

18
00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:45.320
That's right.
确实如此。

19
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:49.900
Well, this was written by Mindy Kaling, directed by Ken Whittingham.
这一集由敏迪·卡灵编剧，肯·威廷汉执导。

20
00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.100
And today, we have a surprise.
今天，我们有个惊喜。

21
00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.180
I'm not reading the summary again today.
我今天不读剧情梗概了。

22
00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.580
Jenna's going to skip out on her duties.
珍娜要逃避她的职责了。

23
00:00:59.020 --> 00:00:59.240
Sorry.
抱歉。

24
00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.400
Jeez, I mean.
天哪，我的意思是。

25
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:01.120
I know.
我知道。

26
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.180
Was I throwing you shade a little bit?
我刚才是在暗讽你吗？

27
00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:03.940
Skip out.
逃避职责。

28
00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:07.700
Well, we have a super fan who wanted to read the summary.
好吧，我们有一位超级粉丝想来读这段梗概。

29
00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.180
For today's episode, it's Terry Carnation.
今天这一集的梗概由特里·卡内申来读。

30
00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:11.340
Terry, welcome.
特里，欢迎你。

31
00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.500
Thank you so much for having me.
非常感谢邀请我来。

32
00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:22.660
I am a huge fan, as you previously stated, of Office Women podcast and you, Jennifer Fisher and Angel.
正如你们刚才所说，我是《办公室》女士播客的超级粉丝，也是你们，詹妮弗·费舍尔和安吉尔的粉丝。

33
00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:30.300
Everything that you guys do and this show, which is just so hysterically funny.
你们所做的一切，还有这个节目，真是太搞笑了。

34
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:36.300
This episode, in particular, I'm so thrilled to be summarizing for your listening pleasure.
特别是这一集，能为各位听众总结剧情，我感到非常激动。

35
00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:38.920
Well, we're happy to have you, Terry.
好吧，很高兴你能来，特里。

36
00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:39.680
Yes.
是的。

37
00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:40.100
Thank you.
谢谢。

38
00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.100
Angela, not Angel, but I appreciate.
是安吉拉，不是安吉尔，但我心领了。

39
00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:43.600
Of course, Angela.
当然是安吉拉。

40
00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:44.600
But you are an angel.
但你确实是个天使（Angel）。

41
00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.560
After all, let's not forget.
毕竟，别忘了这一点。

42
00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.180
Oh, excellent.
哦，太棒了。

43
00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:50.320
Well, should I jump right in, Office Women?
那么，我可以直接开始了吗，《办公室》女士们？

44
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:51.880
Please, let's do it.
请开始吧，我们准备好了。

45
00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:52.500
Excellent.
太好了。

46
00:01:52.900 --> 00:02:07.100
This episode is entitled A Night Away, and it is an excellent episode that features James Halpert and his wife, Pamela.
这一集名为《夜游》，是一集非常精彩的剧集，讲述了詹姆斯·哈尔珀特和他的妻子帕梅拉的故事。

47
00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:12.200
And they are striving to consummate their relationship.
他们正努力圆满他们的关系。

48
00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:21.360
And apparently, there's a young fellow named Dwight Scruti and his best friend, Scott Michael.
显然，还有一个叫德怀特·斯克鲁蒂的年轻人和他的好朋友斯科特·迈克尔。

49
00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.360
They are running across New York City in this episode.
在这一集中，他们正在纽约市四处奔波。

50
00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.700
It seems that Ryan has gotten into a little trouble with the devil's candy.
看起来瑞安因为沾染了“魔鬼糖果”惹上了一点麻烦。

51
00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:33.720
And by that, I mean that fierce little lady, cocaine.
我指的那个凶猛的小女士，就是可卡因。

52
00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.320
Terry, I have a question.
泰瑞，我有个问题。

53
00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:38.400
Have you seen this episode?
你看过这一集吗？

54
00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.180
I haven't seen this episode in particular.
我没看过这一集。

55
00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.800
I have seen an episode of this show.
我看过这剧的一集。

56
00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:47.140
And this is my theory, if I may share it with you two.
这是我的理论，如果我可以和你们俩分享的话。

57
00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:48.740
About the office?
关于办公室的？

58
00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:51.000
The building is possessed.
这栋大楼被附身了。

59
00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:54.340
Why else would the people inside it act the way they do?
不然里面的人为什么会表现得那样？

60
00:02:54.860 --> 00:03:02.120
Why would this delightful Pamela fall in love with that floppy-haired misfit, James Halpert?
为什么可爱的帕梅拉会爱上那个头发软塌塌的怪胎詹姆斯·哈尔珀特？

61
00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:03.720
It makes no sense.
这根本说不通。

62
00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.440
People behaving in just absurd ways.
人们的行为简直荒谬至极。

63
00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.280
The building is possessed.
这栋大楼被附身了。

64
00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.700
The building itself may be a demon.
大楼本身可能就是个恶魔。

65
00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:16.160
And Dwight Scruti himself may be some kind of dybbuk or homunculus.
而德怀特·斯鲁特本人可能是什么迪布克恶灵或人造人。

66
00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:18.560
You think there's paranormal activity.
你觉得有超自然现象。

67
00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:23.400
In fact, several members of the office might be from hell.
事实上，办公室里的几个人可能来自地狱。

68
00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.140
I am here merely to speculate.
我只是在这里推测而已。

69
00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.160
I am saying that perhaps there is a story underneath the story.
我是说，也许故事背后还有故事。

70
00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.440
Yes, this is a light comedy about co-workers.
没错，这是一部关于同事的轻喜剧。

71
00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:31.580
Hardy har har.
哈哈，真好笑。

72
00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:35.720
But underneath it all, there may be something far more nefarious.
但在这之下，可能隐藏着更邪恶的东西。

73
00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:36.700
Wow.
哇。

74
00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.340
Terry, how many episodes have you seen?
泰瑞，你看过几集？

75
00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:40.480
Just the one?
就那一集吗？

76
00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:45.840
I am planning on starting to watch this show as soon as we finish this podcaSt.
我打算在播客录完后就开始看这部剧。

77
00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:47.220
Because it is bewitching me.
因为它让我着迷。

78
00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.140
It has bewitched me.
它已经让我着迷了。

79
00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.080
Okay.
好吧。

80
00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:52.620
So you haven't seen any episodes, then?
所以你一集都没看过？

81
00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:53.740
I have not.
没看过。

82
00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:57.380
And have you listened to any episodes of Dark Air with Terry Carnation?
那你听过《泰瑞·康乃馨的黑暗空气》的任何一集吗？

83
00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:58.820
No, you have not.
不，你没听过。

84
00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:01.100
So we're even, Stephen.
所以我们扯平了，斯蒂芬。

85
00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:01.740
Okay.
好吧。

86
00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.160
Well, I don't think...
嗯，我不觉得……

87
00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:03.820
I think we've...
我觉得我们……

88
00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:07.580
That show, Even Stevens, I have watched every episode of Even Stevens.
那部剧《活宝家族》，我每一集都看过。

89
00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:08.860
Okay.
好吧。

90
00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:12.980
Well, Terry, I think there might have been a miscommunication with your agent.
泰瑞，我觉得你经纪人那边可能沟通有误。

91
00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:13.480
Big fan.
我是大粉丝。

92
00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.140
Huge fan.
超级粉丝。

93
00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:16.320
Thank you so much for having me, Office Women.
非常感谢邀请我来，办公室女士们。

94
00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:20.200
And all of the listeners, thank you for enjoying this show and these two delightful
还有所有的听众，感谢你们喜欢这个节目，以及这两位可爱的

95
00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:25.240
young women as they share their inner torment with you on a weekly basis.
年轻女士每周与你们分享她们内心的煎熬。

96
00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.440
Thank you, Terry Carnation.
谢谢你，泰瑞·康乃馨。

97
00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:31.660
And I'm sure everyone will want to check out Dark Air.
我相信大家都会想去听听《黑暗空气》的。

98
00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:35.020
It's going to premiere April 1st on Audioboom.
它将于4月1日在Audioboom首播。

99
00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:38.660
Terry, we'd love to have you back if you ever start watching the show.
泰瑞，如果你哪天开始看这部剧了，我们很乐意再邀请你。

100
00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.040
If you watch an episode, let us know.
如果你看了哪一集，记得告诉我们。

101
00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:42.200
I really should do that.
我真的应该那么做。

102
00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:43.100
It looks fascinating.
看起来很有意思。

103
00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:44.480
Well, thank you, Terry.
嗯，谢谢你，特里。

104
00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:49.820
There is one young accountant blonde woman who I find very intriguing.
有一位年轻的金发女会计，我觉得她很有魅力。

105
00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:51.760
Oh, boy.
天哪。

106
00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:52.500
Really?
真的吗？

107
00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:55.280
Fictionally speaking.
从虚构的角度来说。

108
00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:57.020
Thank you for having me, Office Women.
谢谢你们邀请我，办公室女士们。

109
00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:58.080
Thank you, Terry.
谢谢你，特里。

110
00:04:58.520 --> 00:04:59.240
Goodbye, Terry.
再见，特里。

111
00:04:59.620 --> 00:04:59.880
Goodbye.
再见。

112
00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.580
Lady, he'd never seen the show.
女士，他根本没看过这部剧。

113
00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:03.100
I don't.
我没看过。

114
00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:04.320
He had no idea what we were talking about.
他根本不知道我们在说什么。

115
00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:07.680
He also sounded suspiciously like Rainn Wilson.
而且他的声音听起来很像雷恩·威尔森。

116
00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:08.880
He really did.
确实很像。

117
00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:09.860
He really did.
真的太像了。

118
00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:11.180
He called me Angel.
他叫我天使。

119
00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.160
Well, that was an adventure.
好吧，那真是一次奇遇。

120
00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.800
We tried something new.
我们尝试了一些新东西。

121
00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:18.440
That was exciting and confusing.
那既令人兴奋又让人困惑。

122
00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:23.460
I feel like we have some phone calls to make after we're done.
我觉得我们录完之后得打几个电话。

123
00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.580
Yeah, I feel like we're going to text some people.
是啊，我觉得我们得给一些人发短信了。

124
00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:26.920
All right.
好的。

125
00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:28.360
Should we get into this episode?
我们要开始聊这一集了吗？

126
00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:30.440
Should you actually read a summary?
你真的要读一下剧情简介吗？

127
00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:31.680
I'd be happy to.
我很乐意。

128
00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:38.080
A lonely Michael and Dwight go to New York City to party with Ryan and meet ladies.
孤独的迈克尔和德怀特去纽约市找瑞安聚会，并结识女性。

129
00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:43.620
In the meantime, the Scranton employees work late to avoid working over the weekend, but
与此同时，斯克兰顿的员工们为了避免周末加班而工作到很晚，但是

130
00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:46.720
they wind up getting locked into the Scranton business park.
他们最终被锁在了斯克兰顿商业园区里。

131
00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.520
And Terry did get this part right.
特里这一点倒是说对了。

132
00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:51.700
Ryan may have a drug problem.
瑞安可能有毒品问题。

133
00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:53.180
Oh, man.
天哪。

134
00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:53.720
Yeah.
是啊。

135
00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.780
What are your fast facts?
你有什么快讯吗？

136
00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:57.660
Here's a fast fact for you, Ange.
安吉，这儿有个快讯给你。

137
00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:01.660
I thought we could do a little breakdown of our guest star, Troy Underbridge.
我想我们可以简单介绍一下我们的客串明星，特洛伊·安德布里奇。

138
00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:03.800
This is his second appearance on the show.
这是他第二次在剧中露面。

139
00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:06.320
You guys know he first showed up in the deposition.
你们知道他第一次出现是在那场取证会上。

140
00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:10.120
He is played by Noel Petock, and we reached out to him.
他由诺埃尔·佩托克饰演，我们联系了他。

141
00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:11.300
Yes, we did.
没错，我们联系了。

142
00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:12.620
And Noel was so sweet.
诺埃尔人非常好。

143
00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:17.300
He sent in a bunch of audio clips, and he had some fun stories to share with us.
他发来了一堆音频片段，还有一些有趣的故事想和我们分享。

144
00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:21.460
Well, the first thing we wanted to know, we asked a lot of our guests, how did he get
我们想知道的第一件事，也是我们问过很多嘉宾的问题，他是怎么得到

145
00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.000
the job on The Office?
《办公室》这份工作的？

146
00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:24.520
And here's what he had to say.
以下是他要说的内容。

147
00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:27.060
Hello, office ladies.
你们好，办公室女士们。

148
00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:28.800
This is Noel Petock.
我是诺埃尔·佩托克。

149
00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:34.620
And I don't recall, really, Allison Jones ever having me audition.
我不记得艾莉森·琼斯曾让我试镜过。

150
00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:39.060
I actually started the whole process doing background through central casting.
我其实是通过中央选角公司做背景演员开始整个过程的。

151
00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:45.340
So I did, I think, just one episode where I did background.
我想我只拍了一集背景角色。

152
00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:50.340
I was not really goofing off, but acted like I was kind of goofing off texting on a phone.
我其实没在偷懒，但演得像是在一边发短信一边偷懒。

153
00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:57.720
I was kind of the posse of Ryan, EJ Novak's character, and had a good time doing it.
我算是EJ·诺瓦克饰演的瑞安的跟班，演得很开心。

154
00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:59.580
I mean, just enjoyed the process.
我是说，我很享受那个过程。

155
00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:06.980
And later down the line, I had gotten a phone call from the assistant director, and she said
后来，我接到了助理导演的电话，她说

156
00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:13.140
she had spoken to Allison Jones and asked me if I'd like to appear on a couple episodes
她和艾莉森·琼斯聊过，问我愿不愿意在几集里

157
00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:13.760
here and there.
露个脸。

158
00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:16.240
But I didn't actually audition.
但我其实并没有试镜。

159
00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:19.180
They just kind of offered me the role, and I gladly accepted.
他们直接给了我这个角色，我欣然接受了。

160
