00:28:17.700 --> 00:28:20.160
And Jim's like, I'm dating Pam.
吉姆说，我在和帕姆约会。

615
00:28:20.380 --> 00:28:22.640
And Michael says, oh, that's still going on?
迈克尔说，哦，你们还在交往？

616
00:28:23.120 --> 00:28:23.600
What?
什么？

617
00:28:25.560 --> 00:28:28.160
So, of course, now Michael has to enlist Dwight.
所以，迈克尔当然只能拉上德怀特了。

618
00:28:28.700 --> 00:28:30.340
And Andy wants to go.
安迪也想去。

619
00:28:30.580 --> 00:28:34.900
He says the old ball and chain has been more chain than ball lately, if you know what I
他说那只“老球与链”最近链子比球还多，如果你懂我的

620
00:28:34.900 --> 00:28:35.080
mean.
意思的话。

621
00:28:35.200 --> 00:28:37.060
I don't know what that means, but it grossed me out.
我不知道那是什么意思，但听得我直犯恶心。

622
00:28:37.300 --> 00:28:40.280
And Angela says, I'm right here, Jenna.
安吉拉说，我就在这儿呢，珍娜。

623
00:28:40.280 --> 00:28:43.800
I would like to call this moment, hello, super pregs.
我想把这一刻称为：你好，超级孕妇。

624
00:28:44.200 --> 00:28:50.760
Six minutes, 52 seconds, I'm standing at front reception, and you can clearly see my maternity
在6分52秒时，我站在前台，你可以清楚地看到我的孕妇装

625
00:28:50.760 --> 00:28:53.200
shirt hanging out from under my sweater.
从毛衣下摆露了出来。

626
00:28:53.480 --> 00:28:54.260
I saw it.
我看到了。

627
00:28:54.680 --> 00:28:54.960
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

628
00:28:55.120 --> 00:28:59.380
And there's a whole blooper that happens right here where I come around from the copier
这里还有一段完整的花絮，我从复印机那边走过来，

629
00:28:59.380 --> 00:29:03.460
laughing, itching, scratching my enormous belly.
一边笑，一边挠着我巨大的肚子。

630
00:29:04.640 --> 00:29:10.260
Well, this all sets the stage for what is going to become Michael and Dwight hitting the
好吧，这一切都为迈克尔和德怀特在纽约的

631
00:29:10.260 --> 00:29:11.120
town in New York.
夜生活做好了铺垫。

632
00:29:11.300 --> 00:29:15.880
They found out from Ryan's assistant that he would be at a club called Prerogative.
他们从瑞安的助理那里打听到他会去一家叫“特权”的夜店。

633
00:29:16.200 --> 00:29:20.820
It's the happiest Ryan has ever been to see Michael or Dwight.
那是瑞安见到迈克尔或德怀特时最高兴的一次。

634
00:29:20.860 --> 00:29:30.180
It's such a funny line because he's so excited to see them that Michael says, Ryan, it's Michael
这句台词太搞笑了，因为他见到他们时太兴奋了，以至于迈克尔说，瑞安，我是迈克尔

635
00:29:30.180 --> 00:29:30.960
and Dwight.
和德怀特。

636
00:29:31.140 --> 00:29:33.680
He's like, I think maybe you haven't seen me clearly.
他就像是说，我觉得你可能没看清是我。

637
00:29:33.680 --> 00:29:34.220
Yeah.
是啊。

638
00:29:34.620 --> 00:29:36.240
He's like, I know it's you guys.
他说，我知道是你们。

639
00:29:36.340 --> 00:29:37.660
And Michael's like, okay.
迈克尔就说，好吧。

640
00:29:40.540 --> 00:29:46.360
Jenna, at eight minutes, 24 seconds, if you love to spot some fun stuff in the background,
珍娜，在8分24秒，如果你喜欢在背景里找乐子的话，

641
00:29:46.640 --> 00:29:51.140
there's some fantastic background dancing by a guy and a blue button down.
有个穿蓝色衬衫的家伙在背景里跳得非常精彩。

642
00:29:51.360 --> 00:29:52.940
He's having the time of his life.
他玩得可开心了。

643
00:29:53.100 --> 00:29:53.740
I love it.
我喜欢这个。

644
00:29:54.020 --> 00:29:58.580
This is also when Ryan is going to introduce us to his friend Troy.
这也是瑞安向我们介绍他朋友特洛伊的时候。

645
00:29:58.940 --> 00:30:01.600
And Dwight says, you look like a hobbit.
德怀特说，你看起来像个霍比特人。

646
00:30:01.600 --> 00:30:08.120
Dwight, he's actually become sort of obsessed with the idea that Troy might actually be from
德怀特，他实际上有点沉迷于特洛伊可能真的来自

647
00:30:08.120 --> 00:30:09.860
the world of the Lord of the Rings.
《指环王》世界的想法。

648
00:30:10.140 --> 00:30:12.160
This is the crazy thing about Dwight.
这就是德怀特疯狂的地方。

649
00:30:12.340 --> 00:30:17.320
And he does this again and again throughout the show where he actually believes in some
他在整部剧中一次又一次地这样做，他真的相信

650
00:30:17.320 --> 00:30:19.580
of this fantastical genre.
这些奇幻题材里的东西。

651
00:30:20.040 --> 00:30:22.720
You know, like, it's crazy to me, but he's earneSt.
你知道吗，这对我来说很疯狂，但他确实是认真的。

652
00:30:23.080 --> 00:30:26.800
He really believes he might be a hobbit and have special powers.
他真的相信自己可能是个霍比特人，还拥有特殊能力。

653
00:30:27.020 --> 00:30:27.240
Yes.
是的。

654
00:30:27.400 --> 00:30:30.940
And of course, anyone with special powers is of great interest to Dwight.
当然，任何拥有特殊能力的人都会引起德怀特的极大兴趣。

655
00:30:30.940 --> 00:30:31.580
Yeah.
没错。

656
00:30:31.780 --> 00:30:38.840
I was really charmed, Angela, by Michael's inability to understand what a bottle service
安吉拉，迈克尔完全搞不懂瓶装酒服务员是做什么的，这真的让我觉得很有趣。

657
00:30:38.840 --> 00:30:39.640
waitress does.
服务员。

658
00:30:39.880 --> 00:30:45.700
This reminded me of you and I when we did go to one nightclub and experienced bottle service
这让我想起了你和我，我们有生以来唯一一次去夜店体验瓶装酒服务的时候。

659
00:30:45.700 --> 00:30:47.020
one time in our lives.
那次经历。

660
00:30:47.300 --> 00:30:49.040
What a joke, okay?
真是个笑话，对吧？

661
00:30:49.640 --> 00:30:51.860
Like, everyone was like, oh, bottle service.
当时每个人都觉得，哦，瓶装酒服务。

662
00:30:51.940 --> 00:30:54.140
And Jenna and I were like, okay, we'd never done this.
我和詹娜当时就想，好吧，我们以前从没试过。

663
00:30:54.280 --> 00:30:57.120
It's like $200 or something.
大概要两百美元还是什么的。

664
00:30:57.120 --> 00:30:58.920
I just remember we got the bill and we're like, what?
我只记得我们拿到账单时，心想，什么鬼？

665
00:30:59.140 --> 00:31:02.300
And they light up this little, like, sparklers.
然后他们点燃了这种小东西，就像仙女棒一样。

666
00:31:02.500 --> 00:31:07.260
They have sparklers and they walk over with a big tray of all of this different type of
他们拿着仙女棒，端着一大托盘各种各样的伏特加或者别的什么酒，

667
00:31:07.260 --> 00:31:08.900
vodka or something and mixers.
还有调酒饮料走过来。

668
00:31:09.320 --> 00:31:11.220
Jenna and I don't drink any of that stuff.
我和詹娜根本不喝那些东西。

669
00:31:11.220 --> 00:31:14.020
So, it was like, what's the point?
所以，这有什么意义呢？

670
00:31:14.020 --> 00:31:16.860
I was hoping there'd be snacks or something.
我当时还指望能有点零食什么的。

671
00:31:17.160 --> 00:31:17.480
No.
并没有。

672
00:31:17.780 --> 00:31:19.400
Like Michael's, same problem.
就像迈克尔一样，问题是一样的。

673
00:31:19.560 --> 00:31:20.460
There's no snacks.
没有零食。

674
00:31:20.640 --> 00:31:23.620
It's just a tray of liquor bottles and mixers.
只有一托盘酒瓶和调酒饮料。

675
00:31:23.820 --> 00:31:24.880
And then here's the thing.
而且重点是这个。

676
00:31:25.220 --> 00:31:29.320
Angela, it's $200, but then you have to make your own drinks.
安吉拉，花了二百美元，结果还得自己调酒。

677
00:31:29.500 --> 00:31:30.780
What's the point of that?
那有什么意义？

678
00:31:30.840 --> 00:31:33.960
I just wanted a cosmopolitan from the bartender.
我只想让调酒师给我调一杯大都会鸡尾酒。

679
00:31:33.960 --> 00:31:36.280
But now I'm trying to make my own drink.
但现在我得试着自己调酒。

680
00:31:36.280 --> 00:31:37.740
I barely know what I'm doing.
我根本不知道自己在干什么。

681
00:31:37.740 --> 00:31:39.500
I was very Michael Scott.
我当时简直就是迈克尔·斯科特。

682
00:31:39.500 --> 00:31:40.580
I'll say that.
我得这么说。

683
00:31:40.840 --> 00:31:45.080
I would have loved a glass of maraschino cherries just to eat them.
我当时要是能有一杯马拉斯奇诺樱桃吃吃就好了。

684
00:31:45.240 --> 00:31:46.280
I was so hungry.
我饿坏了。

685
00:31:46.520 --> 00:31:49.820
I would have loved some chicken fingers and a glass of wine.
我当时要是能来点炸鸡柳配杯红酒就好了。

686
00:31:49.980 --> 00:31:52.240
But now we have sparklers for $200.
结果我们花了二百美元就换来了仙女棒。

687
00:31:52.780 --> 00:31:58.200
I don't know if you guys noticed, but Michael wanted to order a Midori Sour,
不知道你们有没有注意到，迈克尔想点一杯蜜瓜酸酒，

688
00:31:58.520 --> 00:32:04.120
which I thought was an amazing callback to the convention season three.
我觉得这是对第三季会议情节的一个绝妙呼应。

689
00:32:04.660 --> 00:32:07.680
Remember when Jim and Josh had that inside joke?
还记得吉姆和乔什那个内部梗吗？

690
00:32:07.700 --> 00:32:09.040
A shot of Midori, perhaps.
也许来一杯蜜瓜利口酒。

691
00:32:09.380 --> 00:32:13.600
I still think Michael thinks that's a drink that you order when you want to be fancy
我还是觉得迈克尔认为那是你想装高级时会点的酒，

692
00:32:13.600 --> 00:32:14.940
because of Jim and Josh.
就因为吉姆和乔什提过。

693
00:32:15.220 --> 00:32:17.020
This is a way Michael and I are similar.
在这点上我和迈克尔很像。

694
00:32:17.260 --> 00:32:21.300
I would also grab on to a story like that and be like,
我也会抓住这种故事不放，然后心想，

695
00:32:21.420 --> 00:32:24.460
OK, wait, so when I'm in the club, to be cool, order Midori Sour.
好吧，等等，所以当我在夜店时，为了显得酷，就点蜜瓜酸酒。

696
00:32:24.640 --> 00:32:25.020
Got it.
明白了。

697
00:32:25.140 --> 00:32:26.240
And chicken fingers.
还有炸鸡柳。

698
00:32:26.660 --> 00:32:28.080
But there's no chicken fingers.
但那里根本没有炸鸡柳。

699
00:32:28.300 --> 00:32:30.220
You're just going to get a cup of olives.
你只会得到一小杯橄榄。

700
00:32:30.900 --> 00:32:34.240
So meanwhile, back in the office, Jim has some ideas.
与此同时，回到办公室，吉姆有一些想法。

701
00:32:34.620 --> 00:32:38.820
He's a real idea man, even after the whole birthday thing blew up in his face.
他真是个点子王，哪怕生日那件事搞砸了之后也是如此。

702
00:32:39.020 --> 00:32:42.660
His big idea is that if everyone stays late for just a few hours,
他的好点子是，如果大家多留几个小时，

703
00:32:42.840 --> 00:32:44.300
then they won't have to come in tomorrow.
那明天就不用来上班了。

704
00:32:44.640 --> 00:32:49.200
Jim, I hope you were thorough when you decided to suggest this
吉姆，我希望你在提这个建议时考虑周全了，

705
00:32:49.200 --> 00:32:51.680
and that you crossed all your T's and dotted your I's
把所有细节都落实到位了，

706
00:32:51.680 --> 00:32:55.260
because I'm sure people are still pissed off at you about the cakes.
因为我敢肯定大家还在为蛋糕的事生你的气。

707
00:32:55.620 --> 00:32:56.860
I have some news for you.
我有个消息要告诉你。

708
00:32:57.060 --> 00:32:59.300
Angela, he did not do any of that.
安吉拉，他根本没考虑周全。

709
00:32:59.300 --> 00:33:02.420
It turns out that everyone stayed late.
结果就是大家都留下来加班了。

710
00:33:02.420 --> 00:33:05.660
And then at 9 p.m., when they decide to leave,
然后到了晚上九点，当他们决定离开时，

711
00:33:05.820 --> 00:33:08.260
they discover that they are locked into the parking lot.
发现他们被锁在停车场里了。

712
00:33:08.800 --> 00:33:13.020
Yes, lady, there is a fantastic group shot at 8 minutes, 48 seconds
没错，女士，在8分48秒的时候有一个精彩的集体镜头，

713
00:33:13.020 --> 00:33:17.380
where it pans everyone as they realize they're locked in.
镜头扫过每个人，捕捉到他们意识到自己被锁住时的表情。

714
00:33:17.880 --> 00:33:20.920
And I just want you to know, at this point,
而且我想让你知道，此时此刻，

715
00:33:21.040 --> 00:33:24.680
I have reached the point in my pregnancy where I can no longer button up my coat
我的孕期已经到了无法扣上外套扣子的阶段，

716
00:33:25.620 --> 00:33:28.960
and my purse is no longer really hiding my belly.
我的包也再也遮不住我的肚子了。

717
00:33:29.220 --> 00:33:30.700
I have more news for you.
我还有个消息要告诉你。

718
00:33:31.080 --> 00:33:34.520
Not only is the parking gate locked such that they cannot leave,
不仅停车场大门锁住了让他们出不去，

719
00:33:34.720 --> 00:33:37.560
they also cannot return to the comfort of the office
他们也无法回到舒适的办公室里，

720
00:33:37.560 --> 00:33:41.300
because Pam has locked the door from the inside and she doesn't have a key.
因为帕姆从里面锁上了门，而且她没有钥匙。

721
00:33:41.980 --> 00:33:43.380
Pam has a talking head.
帕姆有个访谈镜头。

722
00:33:43.500 --> 00:33:44.800
That is so great.
那太棒了。

723
00:33:44.800 --> 00:33:49.120
She said that Dwight has both the master and spare key.
她说德怀特有主钥匙和备用钥匙。

724
00:33:49.300 --> 00:33:53.060
And when she asked him how they'd get into the office if he ever died,
当她问他如果他死了，他们该怎么进办公室时，

725
00:33:53.380 --> 00:33:54.500
he responded with,
他回答说，

726
00:33:54.800 --> 00:33:55.640
Jenna, you say it.
珍娜，你来说。

727
00:33:55.860 --> 00:33:58.380
If I'm dead, you guys have been dead for weeks.
如果我死了，你们早就死好几周了。

728
00:33:58.700 --> 00:33:59.160
Yeah.
是啊。

729
00:33:59.440 --> 00:34:00.020
Okay, Dwight.
好吧，德怀特。

730
00:34:00.340 --> 00:34:00.620
Okay.
好吧。

731
00:34:00.840 --> 00:34:01.060
Yeah.
是啊。

732
00:34:01.500 --> 00:34:06.060
One of my favorite lines in all of this is Stanley when he declares that
我最喜欢的一句台词是斯坦利说的，他宣称

733
00:34:06.060 --> 00:34:09.300
if he is not in his bath with a glass of wine within the hour,
如果一小时内他没能泡在浴缸里喝上一杯红酒，

734
00:34:09.480 --> 00:34:10.700
they're both dead.
他们两个都死定了。

735
00:34:10.980 --> 00:34:16.800
Now, Jenna, that line to me was the closest to Leslie David Baker in real life
珍娜，我觉得这句台词是莱斯利·大卫·贝克在现实生活中

736
00:34:17.280 --> 00:34:19.880
than any other line he ever said on the show
最真实的一面，比他在剧中说的任何其他台词都更像他本人，

737
00:34:19.880 --> 00:34:24.600
because he and I would talk about how we couldn't wait to get home and take a bath.
因为我们俩经常聊到迫不及待想回家泡个澡。

738
00:34:24.740 --> 00:34:25.940
With a glass of wine.
再来杯红酒。

739
00:34:26.120 --> 00:34:27.300
With a glass of wine.
再来杯红酒。

740
00:34:27.500 --> 00:34:28.980
You know, like soak our muscles.
你知道，就是那种放松肌肉的感觉。

741
00:34:29.260 --> 00:34:31.200
Yes, I thought the same thing, Angela.
是的，安吉拉，我也这么想。

742
00:34:31.980 --> 00:34:33.060
Well, they get an idea.
好吧，他们想到了一个主意。

743
00:34:33.460 --> 00:34:34.380
It's very simple.
很简单。

744
00:34:34.380 --> 00:34:39.420
All we have to do is call the security guard and ask him to come unlock the gate.
我们只需要给保安打电话，让他来开门就行了。

745
00:34:39.600 --> 00:34:39.900
Yeah.
是啊。

746
00:34:40.260 --> 00:34:43.960
But no one has his phone number and no one can remember his name.
但没人有他的电话号码，也没人记得他的名字。

747
00:34:44.180 --> 00:34:44.460
Yeah.
是啊。

748
00:34:44.660 --> 00:34:48.860
No one can remember his name, but Toby has his phone number.
没人记得他的名字，但托比有他的电话号码。

749
00:34:49.020 --> 00:34:53.940
He has his phone number, but he did not enter his name with the phone number into his phone.
他有电话号码，但他没在手机里存名字。

750
00:34:54.080 --> 00:34:59.080
So we still have the name dilemma, but Toby does save the day and Pam is very impressed.
所以我们依然面临名字的难题，但托比确实拯救了大家，帕姆对此印象深刻。

751
00:34:59.380 --> 00:35:02.520
And it's probably Toby's happiest moment in his whole entire life.
这大概是托比一生中最幸福的时刻了。

752
00:35:02.900 --> 00:35:03.380
Yes.
没错。

753
00:35:03.800 --> 00:35:04.060
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

754
00:35:04.380 --> 00:35:07.680
It's going to lead him to make a mistake later, but we'll get there.
这会导致他之后犯错，但我们稍后再说。

755
00:35:08.100 --> 00:35:11.000
Some really big swings are about to come from Toby.
托比接下来会有一些非常大的动作。

756
00:35:13.330 --> 00:35:15.950
We had a fan catch from Ben M.
我们收到了本·M的粉丝投稿。

757
00:35:16.130 --> 00:35:16.990
and Skylar T.
还有斯凯拉·T的。

758
00:35:17.330 --> 00:35:23.710
Can we talk about how Creed is the person who knows Hank's name when nobody else seems to know it?
我们能聊聊为什么克里德是唯一一个知道汉克名字的人吗？明明其他人似乎都不知道。

759
00:35:23.950 --> 00:35:29.050
He seems like the least likely person who would know anyone's name as it has been established.
按照之前的设定，他看起来是最不可能知道别人名字的人。

760
00:35:29.770 --> 00:35:30.930
I just loved that.
我太喜欢这一点了。

761
00:35:31.090 --> 00:35:32.870
I loved it and I thought it was actually perfect.
我喜欢这个设定，我觉得这简直太完美了。

